Apple recently updated the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air</a>, narrowing the gap with the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a>, but how different are the two product lines and which should you buy?<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/03/iPad-Pro-2024-vs-Air-2024-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-998397" /><br/>
Apple has now refreshed the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; with the M4 chip, representing a small update over the previous model from 2025, which introduced the M3 chip. While the upgrade brings improved performance and efficiency, it does not significantly alter the feature set or overall positioning of the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; within the lineup.<br/>
<br/>
By contrast, the &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; continues to sit at the top of Apple's tablet range, now equipped with the latest M5 chip. This update builds on the major redesign introduced in 2024, which brought a substantially thinner and lighter design, tandem OLED display technology, and a range of high-end features aimed at professional workflows. The latest revision focuses more on internal improvements, particularly in GPU performance and AI acceleration, rather than introducing major new capabilities.<br/>
